# ^ The mistboard-engine commit the prod build checks out (railpack build step).
# Fog analyzer runnable on real games (2026-09-05): a314c43 makes the post-game
# fog analyzer usable outside the engine-vs-engine corpus it was tuned on.
# TruthGrader no longer asks Stockfish about a FoW-reachable position where the
# side not to move has a capturable king (STATUS_OPPOSITE_CHECK, how nearly every
# fog game ends): SimpleEngine.analyse takes no timeout and never returns for
# those, so grade()'s except could not fire and the job hung forever. i_sample
# 8 -> 200 (8 missed the truth in its own sample on 20 of 52 plies and charged the
# player a sample_error for each). Belief now uses the resident-Rust state and
# takes a |P| cap, defaulting to production's 16M — uncapped with the Python
# set[str] path passed 8 GiB within seconds on a real game. Also keeps the top-3
# root candidates the solve already computed, for the review's alternatives block.
# LIVE-MOVE RISK: none. Nothing on this ref touches the live turn path; every
# change is inside analysis.py's post-game entry points and scripts/analyze_job.py.
# Rollback target: 91e73d6 (the previous pin; drops the analyzer fixes only, no
# registry or env changes).
#
# fdx v1.2, time-bounded search (2026-09-05): 6f16bfd (carried by a314c43) adds the
# guarded-timed-i32-20m bundle and engine id python-fdx-v1.2. v1.1's search was
# iteration-bounded, not time-bounded — the loop ran range(64) and the deadline
# break inside solve_multiroot_rust_tree was unreachable, so Misty played a full
# 5+5 game in 24.4s of thinking (~1.8% of the offered budget) and finished with
# more clock than it started. v1.2 lifts the cap out of reach and adds a 4s
# per-move ceiling, so wall time is the real control. v1.0/v1.1 are frozen and
# byte-identical; DMX is untouched (the shared budget helper's new max_seconds
# defaults to None). Rollback target: 91e73d6 — but note that reverting the pin
# alone strands the web registry, which offers python-fdx-v1.2; roll web back
# to the commit before the v1.2 registration, or the worker falls through to
# the STRIPPED legacy bundle and silently serves a weaker bot.
#
# Rides along, benign: 91e73d6..a314c43 also carries jungle/viewer/lab/docs
# commits (b8c7532, 91e04b3, 1caeba2, 39a3805, 4083d74, 18cfe4a, 40f69a1) plus
# a314c43 itself (fog analyzer runnable on real games: analyze_job.py +
# analysis.py). None touch scripts/live_move_worker.py, the live path does not
